      "flaw_name": "Constraint Sequencing Capture",
      "defect_type": "Type I",
      "severity": 2,
      "explanation": "The Department defers competition until 2027 and uses that sequencing problem to justify continuing the incumbent now, but the notice does not meaningfully compare less competition-limiting bridge structures.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "section": "Background / Waivers and Extensions",
          "quote_or_absence": "The available record says there is not enough time in FY 2026 to carry out a full, robust competitive process and therefore proposes a continuation award for the currently funded 84.351A project."
        }
      ],
      "comment_leverage": "Ask why a shorter or more limited interim competitive path was unavailable and what prevents future repeat extensions."
    },
    {
      "flaw_key": "evidence_to_intrusion_mismatch",
      "flaw_name": "Evidence-to-Intrusion Mismatch",
      "defect_type": "Type II",
      "severity": 2,
      "explanation": "The proposal makes a real allocation choice in favor of the incumbent, but the public record gives only a high-level necessity showing for why no competition-preserving alternative could be used in FY 2026.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "section": "Background",
          "quote_or_absence": "The available record states that the appropriations act was enacted later than expected and that there is not enough time in FY 2026, but it does not provide a detailed schedule analysis."
        }
      ],
      "comment_leverage": "Ask for the actual timeline and the rejected options that support the Department's necessity claim."
